{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_14_research_phase3_referee", "label": "Research Pipeline Phase 3: the Referee \u2014 Implementation Plan", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The referee still keeps research.handoff=false because nothing is admitted without a tested thesis (phase 4)."}, {"id": "trader_research_portfolio_null", "label": "trader/research/portfolio_null.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A market-wide condition breaks the per-symbol independence assumption: the binomial counts one regime effect 19 times, so the referee needs a test whose unit of evidence is the whole book of entries."}, {"id": "trader_research_fdr", "label": "trader/research/fdr.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "LORD++ spends fastest early; twin-dedupe and the untestable pre-check exist to keep junk from spending the budget."}, {"id": "trader_research_referee", "label": "trader/research/referee.py", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One candidate spends one test: the gate-1 p-value is the MAXIMUM of the p-values it has to clear, which is a valid p-value for the intersection hypothesis, so LORD++ is charged once, not three times."}, {"id": "trader_research_null_baseline_consistency_p_dependent", "label": "consistency_p_dependent()", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trade-outcome correlation was not used because trades on different symbols have no common alignment; the matched-offset null does, and percentile correlation bounds the clear/not-clear indicator correlation from above."}, {"id": "concept_lord_plus_plus", "label": "LORD++ online FDR control", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Target fdr_target=0.10, lord_w0=0.05; the alpha sequence lives in the ledger and survives restarts, and a forward brake halves alpha_t while more than 10% of finished windows failed."}, {"id": "concept_common_rotation_null", "label": "Common-rotation null", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shifts every symbol's entries by the SAME offset, keeping cross-symbol clustering intact; its statistic is the portfolio's compounded return under the live cap, because that is the quantity the book is judged on."}, {"id": "concept_consistency_p", "label": "consistency_p cross-symbol consistency test", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-14-research-phase3-referee.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assumes each symbol's null percentile is an independent vote; a market-wide condition breaks that assumption, so the binomial can count one effect n times."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_superpowers_plans_2026_09_14_research_phase3_referee", "target": "docs_superpowers_plans